{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>In the selfsame day</b> Rashi wrote: \"In the selfsame day — that Abraham completed ninety-nine years and Ishmael thirteen, they were circumcised.\" But what is the reason to mention this? Moreover, they already agreed (Rosh HaShanah 10a) according to Rabbi Eliezer's opinion that the world was created in Tishrei, and in Tishrei the patriarchs were born, and at Passover Isaac was born, and Scripture says, \"at the set time of this year in the next\" (Genesis 18:10), and he [Rashi] himself wrote in the portion of Vayera (Genesis 18:10) that the tidings were at Passover and at the following Passover Isaac was born. Rather, \"in the selfsame day\" means that on the very day he was commanded regarding this mitzvah, he circumcised himself and the homeborn of his household, eighteen and three hundred, and all those bought with his money. Scripture recounts his merit in the fear of YHWH and the merit of all the members of his household, that all of them were zealous and early to perform mitzvot. And there is no difficulty in the verse \"Abraham was circumcised\" (Genesis 17:26), that he was circumcised first, for actually Ishmael his son was circumcised first, and all the members of his household, as it is written (Genesis 17:23), \"And Abraham took Ishmael his son and all the homeborn of his household,\" and afterward, \"and Abraham was ninety-nine years old when he was circumcised\" (Genesis 17:24). The reason is that Abraham was zealous regarding their circumcision first and circumcised them himself, or he arranged many mohalim for them while he stood over them, and only afterward circumcised himself — for had he performed his own circumcision first, he would have been ill or endangered by it on account of his old age and would not have been able to attend to their circumcision:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:30:37.813505697Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}